### bind-parameter-e2e.http
###
### docs/plans/bind-parameter-steel-thread-plan.md WI-8 — checked-in record of
### the end-to-end verification run against a live API + real PostgreSQL, per
### the plan's own instruction not to leave a third undocumented manual e2e
### step (after phase-drawn WI-8 and create-competition WI-7, both of which
### were manual and left no record).
###
### This file was executed for real on 2026-08-08 against:
###   - a throwaway Postgres 16 container (docker run postgres:16-alpine)
###   - `dotnet run --project src/Soarscore.Api --urls http://localhost:5299`
### and every response below matches what the run actually returned. It is
### also intended to be re-run as a regression check: start the two processes
### above, open this file in Rider's HTTP Client, and run top to bottom.
###
### Two companion body files sit next to this one — `publish-f5k-body.json`
### and `publish-nz-m-ales200-body.json`. Each wraps the corresponding real
### seed definition (tools/Soarscore.SeedData/json/40-f5k.json and
### /80-nz-m-ales200.json) in the `{"definition": {...}}` envelope
### `PublishClassDefinition` actually requires — POSTing the raw seed file
### unwrapped 500s with a NullReferenceException in
### ClassDefinitionIngestion.CheckLimits, confirmed while building this file.
### If either seed file changes, regenerate its wrapped copy here.
###
### IMPORTANT FINDING FROM THIS RUN, not fixed by this thread and not this
### thread's job to fix: the plan's own text says "publish F5K ... attempt
### the draw (expect drawPhase.parameterUnbound)". Run for real, F5K's real
### definition does NOT reach that failure. Both of F5K's phases are
### ChooseFromCatalogue (5-task catalogues), which trips
### `drawPhase.unsupportedRoundComposition` in Competition.DrawPhase before
### the parameter-binding check is ever reached — a separate, pre-existing,
### deliberately out-of-scope gap (the plan's "Finding 1"). Binding
### `minPerGroup` cannot unblock F5K's draw today. This is exactly what
### BindParameterEventStoreTests.cs (WI-7) found and worked around by using
### NZ Class M ALES 200's real definition for its store-backed payoff test
### instead of F5K's. This file does the same: it runs F5K far enough to
### demonstrate that finding for real (steps 1-4), then runs the plan's full
### intended sequence — parameterUnbound -> BindParameter -> success —
### against NZ Class M ALES 200 (steps 5-14), one of the other two classes
### this thread names as unblocked (F5K, F5L, NZ Class M ALES 200 all carry a
### no-default minPerGroup/groupSize parameter).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5299

### =====================================================================
### Part 1 — F5K: publish, create, attempt the draw. Demonstrates the
### catalogue-choice limitation above; does NOT reach parameterUnbound.
### =====================================================================

### 1. Publish F5K's real class definition.
### Actual response in this run: 200, body
###   "b064045339205123fe297b8068535270e3e6aff69cd9b780418856bcf6853986"
POST {{baseUrl}}/publish-class-definition
Content-Type: application/json

< ./publish-f5k-body.json

> {%
    client.global.set("f5kHash", JSON.parse(response.body));
%}

### 2. Create a competition adopting F5K.
### Actual response: 200, body {"value":"019fdfc7-df8a-7346-81fa-6823b46e777a"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/create-competition
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "F5K E2E Test",
  "location": "Taupo",
  "startDate": "2026-01-10",
  "endDate": "2026-01-12",
  "classContentHash": "{{f5kHash}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("f5kCompId", JSON.parse(response.body).value);
%}

### 3a. Register one person — enough to attempt a draw (the draw fails on
### round composition before it would ever check the field size).
POST {{baseUrl}}/register-person
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Pilot F5K",
  "contact": { "email": "pilot-f5k-1@example.com" },
  "club": null
}

> {%
    client.global.set("f5kPersonId", JSON.parse(response.body).value);
%}

### 3b. Register that person as a competitor.
POST {{baseUrl}}/register-competitor
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "competitionId": { "value": "{{f5kCompId}}" },
  "personId": { "value": "{{f5kPersonId}}" }
}

### 4. Attempt the draw.
### Actual response in this run: 400
###   {"type":"https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc9110#section-15.5.1",
###    "title":"drawPhase.unsupportedRoundComposition","status":400,
###    "detail":"This phase's round composition (multi-task rounds or
###    catalogue task choice) is not yet supported by the draw.", ...}
### NOT drawPhase.parameterUnbound — see the file header. Binding minPerGroup
### here would not change this outcome, so this thread's F5K leg stops here.
POST {{baseUrl}}/draw-phase
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "competitionId": { "value": "{{f5kCompId}}" },
  "rounds": 2
}

### =====================================================================
### Part 2 — NZ Class M ALES 200: the plan's actual provable sequence.
### NZ-M's real definition (unlike F5K's) is FixedSequence/single-task on
### its one phase, so it reaches drawPhase.parameterUnbound and can be
### unblocked by BindParameter, exactly as WI-7's store-backed payoff test
### (BindParameterEventStoreTests.cs,
### BindParameter_unblocks_DrawPhase_for_NZ_Class_M_ALES_200_...) already
### proves against a real Postgres store. This section repeats that proof
### through the live HTTP API end to end.
### =====================================================================

### 5. Publish NZ Class M ALES 200's real class definition.
### Actual response: 200, body
###   "0cb1bb1cf79e8411ae378b2fc6fcabe5b424b277d42469527b3373e9ef0dabd0"
POST {{baseUrl}}/publish-class-definition
Content-Type: application/json

< ./publish-nz-m-ales200-body.json

> {%
    client.global.set("nzmHash", JSON.parse(response.body));
%}

### 6. Create a competition adopting NZ Class M ALES 200.
### Actual response: 200, body {"value":"019fdfc8-3499-7200-adee-f9cec81fd6cc"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/create-competition
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "NZ-M ALES 200 E2E Test",
  "location": "Taupo",
  "startDate": "2026-01-10",
  "endDate": "2026-01-12",
  "classContentHash": "{{nzmHash}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("nzmCompId", JSON.parse(response.body).value);
%}

### 7. Register 12 people + competitors — enough to satisfy a groupSize of 6
### (two full groups). Run 1..12: this block reuses the same "nzmPersonId"
### variable for each pair, since only the just-registered person is needed
### to register that pilot's competitor before moving to the next pilot.
###
